Based on my review of the diff and plan, I have a clear understanding of this change. It involves:

1. **`scripts/ship-pr.sh`** - Major refactor: deferred-push rebase in CI-fix path, vendor waterfall rotation, fork-aware base threading
2. **`scripts/hook-anti-read-poll.sh`** - Significantly expanded to handle Bash task-output polling (Read|Bash matcher)
3. **`scripts/ci-behind-count.sh`** - New shared helper extracted from `ci-status.sh`
4. **`scripts/git-sync-local-main.sh`** - Extended with `--base-remote`/`--base-ref` params
5. **Documentation updates** - AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG, docs/workflow-lifecycle.md

{"archetypes":[{"name":"ship-pr-state-machine","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The CI-fix path has new global mutable state (CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING), complex control flow around deferred-push rebases, and multiple return-code paths that must be propagated without loss — correctness in this state machine is the highest risk.","prompt_body":"Focus on correctness of the CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING flag lifecycle in scripts/ship-pr.sh: when it is set, when it is cleared, and whether every code path that sets it true also has a corresponding clear on success. Examine whether the pending_retry branch (lines ~1459–1541) correctly skips token-record append and vendor capture phases. Verify that _run_post_rebase_verify_gates returns and the caller maps return codes (0/2/4/other) consistently — look for off-by-one or swapped rc mappings. Check whether a failed git-force-push after a deferred rebase leaves CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING=true as intended and whether subsequent retries can still clear it. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-parse-robustness","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new hook-anti-read-poll.sh Bash segment parser handles quote-state tracking, shell-operator splitting, and variable expansion in pure Bash — subtle off-by-one or missed quote-toggle cases could produce false positives or false negatives that suppress the intended anti-polling warning.","prompt_body":"Examine scripts/hook-anti-read-poll.sh's bash_line_task_output_poll_tokens function: check whether the quote-state toggles (in_s/in_d/in_b) handle escaped characters, nested backtick-in-double-quote, or EOF-without-segment-flush correctly. Verify that bash_expand_simple_var_refs handles the renderer-substitution safety comment correctly (lint-renderer-safe pragma) and that global-replace via ${line//\"$ref\"/$val} is safe when $val contains & or \\ under the macOS Bash 3.2 version. Check whether bash_normalize_cmd's sed continuation-folding handles trailing whitespace before the backslash correctly. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fork-base-threading","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The deferred-rebase path adds base_remote/base_ref threading through run_rebase_rebump, _run_rebase_rebump_from_step3, _run_rebase_rebump_verify_plain_no_push, and git-sync-local-main.sh — a missed pass-through at any call site silently reverts fork targets to origin/main.","prompt_body":"Trace every call site of run_rebase_rebump in scripts/ship-pr.sh to confirm that each invocation that may run in a fork context correctly passes base_remote and base_ref (not just the new deferred-rebase site). Check that _run_rebase_rebump_from_step3's git show invocation uses ${base_remote}/${base_ref} for the version-regression check and that git-sync-local-main.sh passes those args correctly. Verify that LAST_STAGE_AND_PUSH_PRE_REFRESH_HEAD is refreshed after the deferred rebase so the no-commit bail check uses the post-rebase HEAD, not the pre-rebase HEAD. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"rebase-count-invariant","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The deferred-push branch inside _run_rebase_rebump_from_step3 skips the REBASE_COUNT increment — this diverges from the non-deferred branch and could allow infinite deferred-rebase storms if the caller never increments the cap counter.","prompt_body":"Check scripts/ship-pr.sh _run_rebase_rebump_from_step3: in the defer_push=true branch, REBASE_COUNT is not incremented (only ITERATION and TRANSIENT_RETRIES are updated). Verify whether the calling path in _stage_and_push_ci_fixes checks the REBASE_COUNT cap before calling run_rebase_rebump, or whether the cap check inside run_rebase_rebump itself fires before _run_rebase_rebump_from_step3 is entered. If the cap check runs before the internal function, confirm that increments are consistent across both branches. Identify any scenario where a rebase loop could proceed past the 20-rebase cap because of the skipped increment in the deferred-push path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-behind-count-extraction","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"ci-status.sh now delegates behind-count computation to ci-behind-count.sh with --no-fetch, relying on a prior fetch at line 80 — if that fetch was made to a different remote/ref than what the helper receives, the count could be silently wrong.","prompt_body":"Verify in scripts/ci-status.sh that the remote and ref passed to ci-behind-count.sh --no-fetch exactly match the remote and ref that were fetched earlier in ci-status.sh (around line 80). Check whether ci-status.sh's awk-based BEHIND_COUNT extraction handles multi-line output or a missing BEHIND_COUNT= line safely (falls back to 0). In scripts/ship-pr.sh's _stage_and_push_ci_fixes, confirm that ci-behind-count.sh is called without --no-fetch so it performs its own fetch rather than relying on a potentially stale remote state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
